<newsitem itemid="196008" id="root" date="1996-11-18" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Barlows year shr rises 27 percent.</title>
<headline>Barlows year shr rises 27 percent.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     329.2	 vs 259.7</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 105	   vs 84</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   666.9	 vs 528.1</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   1,041.8     vs 919.5</p>
<p>    Tax			 260.5	 vs 301.3</p>
<p>    Interest received     46.5	  vs 68.7</p>
<p>    Turnover		  17,810.7    vs 15,521.6</p>
<p>Div payable January 13</p>
<p>on register December 6</p>
<p>Full name: Barlow Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast earnings before exceptional items to rise to between 325 and 330 cents per share with a consensus of 326.7 cents.</p>
<p>	  -- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
